@@ -2,17 +2,18 @@
   "slug": "item-upgrades",
   "title": "Item upgrades",
   "summary": "Turn matching copies into a higher quality, with the right recipe for each system.",
-  "body": "<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at <strong>Ascended</strong>, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at <strong>Ascension</strong>. They have separate item definitions. Match the exact item and quality.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recipes\">Upgrade recipes</h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><caption>Guaranteed upgrades with no coin fee</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Input</th><th scope=\"col\">Result</th><th scope=\"col\">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 identical Base zone rewards</th><td>1 Polished</td><td>#zoneforge only</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Polished copies</th><td>1 Exalted</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Exalted copies</th><td>1 Ascended ordinary item, or 1 Ascension zone reward</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"box\">Get the reusable Reforging Box</h2><ol><li>Hail <strong>Artisan Veyra</strong> in the East Commonlands tunnel for a free Reforging Box.</li><li>Put the box in a main inventory slot. Leave combat and casting, empty your cursor, and close trade, loot, merchant and station interactions.</li><li>Place four identical eligible Polished or Exalted copies in the box. This is a container combine, not an NPC hand-in.</li><li>Press Combine. A valid recipe consumes the four copies and gives one next-quality item; keep the box for later.</li></ol><p>The box has no Base recipe and no recipe above the top tier. Bags cannot be nested in the box. The supported-item catalog determines eligibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Before combining</h2><p>Use unmodified items of one family and quality. Socketed, dyed, ornamented, customized and evolving instances are not eligible. Binding is preserved. Charged objects count as physical items, not as one copy per charge. If a result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and contact the owner.</p>\n<h2 id=\"other-upgrades\">Keep other systems separate</h2><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Ascension</a> uses its own quest and materials. <a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Ordinary tradeskills</a> retain recipe requirements and success chances. The top-tier names do not mean those systems share recipes.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Dungeon rewards</a> use Normal, Polished and Ascended qualities but have no conversion through these recipes. Earn their qualities through Grind or Raid completion and Raid final-boss drops.</p>",
+  "body": "<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at <strong>Ascended</strong>, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at <strong>Ascension</strong>. They have separate item definitions. Match the exact item and quality.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recipes\">Upgrade recipes</h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><caption>Guaranteed upgrades with no coin fee</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Input</th><th scope=\"col\">Result</th><th scope=\"col\">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 identical Base zone rewards</th><td>1 Polished</td><td>#zoneforge only</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Polished copies</th><td>1 Exalted</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Exalted copies</th><td>1 Ascended ordinary item, or 1 Ascension zone reward</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"box\">Get the reusable Reforging Box</h2><ol><li>Hail <strong>Artisan Veyra</strong> in the East Commonlands tunnel for a free Reforging Box.</li><li>Put the box in a main inventory slot. Leave combat and casting, empty your cursor, and close trade, loot, merchant and station interactions.</li><li>Place four identical eligible Polished or Exalted copies in the box. This is a container combine, not an NPC hand-in.</li><li>Press Combine. A valid recipe consumes the four copies and gives one next-quality item; keep the box for later.</li></ol><p>The live box has no Base recipe yet and no recipe above the top tier. See the pending normal-item recipe below. Bags cannot be nested in the box. The supported-item catalog determines eligibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"normal-items\">Normal items: update awaiting release</h2><p><strong>Not released:</strong> the Reforging Box update accepts exactly <strong>3 identical eligible Normal (Base) items → 1 Polished item</strong>, for ordinary tiered equipment and Classic zone-hunt rewards. Put the three copies in the reusable box, leave its fourth slot empty, and press Combine. A matching Polished version must exist. The higher recipes still cost four copies. Stackable units count individually; nonstackable charged items count once each. Dungeon rewards and bags remain excluded. Deployment and in-game confirmation are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Before combining</h2><p>Use unmodified items of one family and quality. Socketed, dyed, ornamented, customized and evolving instances are not eligible. Binding is preserved. Charged objects count as physical items, not as one copy per charge. If a result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and contact the owner.</p>\n<h2 id=\"other-upgrades\">Keep other systems separate</h2><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Ascension</a> uses its own quest and materials. <a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Ordinary tradeskills</a> retain recipe requirements and success chances. The top-tier names do not mean those systems share recipes.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Dungeon rewards</a> use Normal, Polished and Ascended qualities but have no conversion through these recipes. Earn their qualities through Grind or Raid completion and Raid final-boss drops.</p>",
