   "title": "Zone hunt & forging",
   "summary": "Find new rewards, socket heroic augments and forge the next quality.",
-  "body": "<p>Forty-eight enabled Classic combat zones offer a new augment family and an equipment family. The release is installed for live testing. Explore the <a href=\"zones.html\">zone directory</a> or <a href=\"items.html\">item index</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"drops\">How drops work</h2><p>Each eligible native enemy has two independent rolls: <strong>0.5% for its zone augment</strong> and <strong>0.5% for its zone equipment</strong>. Both may drop together. Ordinary loot remains. Each family averages one reward per 200 eligible kills, with no guarantee or pity counter.</p><table><caption>Quality after a successful family roll</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Quality</th><th scope=\"col\">Chance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Base</td><td>60%</td></tr><tr><td>Polished</td><td>30%</td></tr><tr><td>Exalted</td><td>8%</td></tr><tr><td>Ascension</td><td>2%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only approved native enemies qualify. Cities, hubs, merchants, pets and summoned copies do not. Kithicor requires eligible nighttime undead.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sockets\">Sockets &amp; heroic stats</h2><p>Eligible head, arms, hands, chest, legs and feet armor has a type-22 socket for these augments. Existing sockets remain. Required levels and compatibility still apply.</p><p>At level 50, every two effective heroic INT from these socketed augments adds one point to the item Spell Damage cap, up to +30. Heroic WIS does the same for Healing Amount. With the current base cap of 250, either can reach 280. Increasing a cap does not grant the underlying bonus; you still need enough actual Spell Damage or Healing Amount equipped.</p>\n<h2 id=\"forging\">Forge matching rewards into the next quality</h2><ol><li>Carry three identical Base rewards, or four identical Polished or Exalted rewards, unequipped and unmodified.</li><li>Leave combat, empty your cursor, and close loot, trade and merchant windows.</li><li>Type <code>#zoneforge</code> and choose the named upgrade.</li></ol><p><strong>3 Base → 1 Polished; 4 Polished → 1 Exalted; 4 Exalted → 1 Ascension.</strong> There is no fee or random failure. Different zones and qualities cannot mix. Socketed, dyed, ornamented, customized or evolving items cannot be inputs. Ascension is the final quality.</p><p>For Polished and Exalted rewards, Artisan Veyra’s <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#box\">Reforging Box</a> offers the same four-copy upgrades. The box also supports eligible ordinary tiered gear.</p>\n<h2 id=\"trade\">Trading &amp; resale</h2><p>These rewards can be traded between players but have <strong>no merchant resale value</strong>. If an upgrade result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and tell the owner what happened.</p>",
+  "body": "<p>Forty-eight enabled Classic combat zones offer a new augment family and an equipment family. The release is installed for live testing. Explore the <a href=\"zones.html\">zone directory</a> or <a href=\"items.html\">item index</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"drops\">How drops work</h2><p>Each eligible native enemy has two independent rolls: <strong>0.5% for its zone augment</strong> and <strong>0.5% for its zone equipment</strong>. Both may drop together. Ordinary loot remains. Each family averages one reward per 200 eligible kills, with no guarantee or pity counter.</p><table><caption>Quality after a successful family roll</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Quality</th><th scope=\"col\">Chance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Base</td><td>60%</td></tr><tr><td>Polished</td><td>30%</td></tr><tr><td>Exalted</td><td>8%</td></tr><tr><td>Ascension</td><td>2%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only approved native enemies qualify. Cities, hubs, merchants, pets and summoned copies do not. Kithicor requires eligible nighttime undead.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sockets\">Sockets &amp; heroic stats</h2><p>Eligible head, arms, hands, chest, legs and feet armor has a type-22 socket for these augments. Existing sockets remain. Required levels and compatibility still apply.</p><p>At level 50, every two effective heroic INT from these socketed augments adds one point to the item Spell Damage cap, up to +30. Heroic WIS does the same for Healing Amount. With the current base cap of 250, either can reach 280. Increasing a cap does not grant the underlying bonus; you still need enough actual Spell Damage or Healing Amount equipped.</p>\n<h2 id=\"forging\">Forge matching rewards into the next quality</h2><ol><li>Carry three identical Base rewards, or four identical Polished or Exalted rewards, unequipped and unmodified.</li><li>Leave combat, empty your cursor, and close loot, trade and merchant windows.</li><li>Type <code>#zoneforge</code> and choose the named upgrade.</li></ol><p><strong>3 Base → 1 Polished; 4 Polished → 1 Exalted; 4 Exalted → 1 Ascension.</strong> There is no fee or random failure. Different zones and qualities cannot mix. Socketed, dyed, ornamented, customized or evolving items cannot be inputs. Ascension is the final quality.</p><p>For Polished and Exalted rewards, Artisan Veyra’s <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#box\">Reforging Box</a> offers the same four-copy upgrades. The box also supports eligible ordinary tiered gear. A <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">pending box update</a> adds the same three-Base-to-Polished step; it is not live yet.</p>\n<h2 id=\"trade\">Trading &amp; resale</h2><p>These rewards can be traded between players but have <strong>no merchant resale value</strong>. If an upgrade result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and tell the owner what happened.</p>",
